<section id="S11" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">11 </span>Additional Backbone Ablation</h2>

<div id="S11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In addition to <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 Backbone Ablation ‣ 4 Results ‣ DSFlash: Comprehensive Panoptic Scene Graph Generation in Realtime" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>, we provide additional backbone ablation results. <a href="#S11.F10" title="In 11 Additional Backbone Ablation ‣ DSFlash: Comprehensive Panoptic Scene Graph Generation in Realtime" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> shows how DSFlash’s scene graph performance correlates with the panoptic quality (<em id="S11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">PQ</em>) of the segmentation model.
Using EoMT2 models (<em id="S11.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">i.e</em>.<span id="S11.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text"></span> pretrained with DINOv2) as the backbone for DSFlash results in slightly worse results than EoMT3 models.
We also observe a very strong correlation of 0.99 between <em id="S11.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">mR@inf</em> and <em id="S11.p1.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">PQ</em>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S11.F10" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S11.F10.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2603.10538v1/backbone-impact2.png" id="S11.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:685/514;" width="685" height="514" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S11.F10.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2603.10538v1/backbone-impact2-pq.png" id="S11.F10.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:685/514;" width="685" height="514" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S11.F10.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 10</span>: </span><span id="S11.F10.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Correlation of scene graph performance (<em id="S11.F10.6.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">mR@50</em>) and backbone capabilities (measured in <em id="S11.F10.6.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">mR@inf</em> and panoptic quality).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S11.F11" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.10538v1/backbone-lowres2.png" id="S11.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/343;" width="548" height="343" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S11.F11.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 11</span>: </span><span id="S11.F11.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Comparison of the effect of low-resolution segmentation masks on the final performance and latency when using different segmentation backbones.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S12" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">12 </span>Train with pruned patches/token merging</h2>

<div id="S12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S12.T5" title="In 12 Train with pruned patches/token merging ‣ DSFlash: Comprehensive Panoptic Scene Graph Generation in Realtime" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> shows RPS measurements on different hardware.
Considering the drop in <em id="S12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">mR@50</em>, there are only minor throughput gains on an H100 and RTX 3090.
On a GTX 1080, RPS improves by about 25% compared to the baseline experiment when combining patch pruning and token merging.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S12.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S12.T5.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 5</span>: </span><span id="S12.T5.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Impact of Token Merging (<em id="S12.T5.6.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">ToMe</em>) and mask-based dynamic patch pruning (<em id="S12.T5.6.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Prune</em>, <a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4 Mask-Based Dynamic Patch Pruning ‣ 3 Method ‣ DSFlash: Comprehensive Panoptic Scene Graph Generation in Realtime" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>) on DSFlash’s RPS, measured on a H100, RTX 3090, and GTX 1080 GPU.</span></figcaption>
<table id="S12.T5.7" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S12.T5.7.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S12.T5.7.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Prune</th>
<th id="S12.T5.7.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">ToMe</th>
<th id="S12.T5.7.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">H100</th>
<th id="S12.T5.7.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">3090</th>
<th id="S12.T5.7.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">1080</th>
<th id="S12.T5.7.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">mR@50</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S12.T5.7.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S12.T5.7.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="S12.T5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S12.T5.7.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_t">0%</td>
<td id="S12.T5.7.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_t">28,663</td>
<td id="S12.T5.7.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_t">11,491</td>
<td id="S12.T5.7.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_t">671</td>
<td id="S12.T5.7.2.6" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_right ltx_border_t">28.80</td></tr>
<tr id="S12.T5.7.3" class="ltx_tr">
